# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  NEVER COMMIT SIGNING KEYS.
#
#  If your private key leaks, anyone can mint valid licenses for
#  your extension — and because verification is offline, you have
#  no way to revoke them. There is no recovery from this.
#
#  Keep the private key outside the repo entirely (a password
#  manager plus offline media). These rules are a seatbelt, not
#  a substitute for that.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*private*
*PRIVATE*
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
keys-*.csv
licenses-*.csv
*SECRET*
*secret*
.env
.env.*

# Real deployment config (the template in this repo is safe; a
# filled-in copy is not — it carries your webhook secret and
# spreadsheet IDs).
*-READY.gs
*-ready.gs

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Node (only if you add tooling later)
node_modules/

# test artefacts (contain real keys)
tools/keys/
tools/_testdata.js
